Enhancement: Inspect directory entries concurrently in `backup`

The `backup` command inspected one file or directory at a time. On network
filesystems such as NFS and SMB, every stat and extended attribute read waits
for a round trip to the server, so backups of directories with many unchanged
files were slow even when no file had to be read.

Restic now supports `backup --walk-concurrency n`, or the environment variable
`RESTIC_WALK_CONCURRENCY`, to inspect up to `n` directory entries at the same
time. The scan that computes the size of the backup for the progress output
uses the same concurrency, so it finishes before the backup does. The default
of 1 keeps the previous behavior. The stored trees are the same for any value.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/2275
